## Location
rust/lichen-rpl/src/dodag.rs:301-308

## Issue
When a root demotes via `demote()`, only `role`, `preferred_parent`, `rank`, and `parents` are reset. `lowest_rank` retains its value (was `min_hop_rank_increase` from root creation).

```rust
pub fn demote(&mut self) {
    if self.role == DodagRole::Root {
        self.role = DodagRole::Unjoined;
        self.preferred_parent = None;
        self.rank = INFINITE_RANK;
        self.parents.clear();
        // lowest_rank NOT reset
        // version NOT reset
    }
}
```

## Trigger
1. Create root with `min_hop_rank_increase = 256`, so `lowest_rank = 256`
2. Call `demote()` -> node is Unjoined but `lowest_rank = 256`
3. Process a DIO from a neighbor at rank 1000, with link_etx = 2.0
4. Path cost = 1000 + 512 = 1512
5. Admissibility check: `cost <= lowest_rank + max_rank_increase` = `1512 <= 256 + 1024` = `1512 <= 1280` = FALSE

The demoted node cannot rejoin via a parent that would be valid for a fresh node.

## Impact
A demoted root cannot rejoin the DODAG through parents it should be able to accept, because `lowest_rank` is artificially constrained to its former root rank.

## Suggested fix
```rust
pub fn demote(&mut self) {
    if self.role == DodagRole::Root {
        self.role = DodagRole::Unjoined;
        self.preferred_parent = None;
        self.rank = INFINITE_RANK;
        self.lowest_rank = INFINITE_RANK;  // ADD
        self.parents.clear();
    }
}
```
